The way to find these scrap dealers is to visit them.  Look at your
yellow pages under "Scrap Metal" and call these places.  Drive around.
Look for the surplus property disposal arms of defense contractors,
universities, and unsupervised Boy Scouts.  Read.  Talk to other
collectors of minicomputers and junque in your area.  Post to local
newsgroups, form a bond with a few dozen people.  Everything I've
found has been by word of mouth - or a little leg-work.  Talk to old
hams.  Or young ones, if there are any left.  Keep your eyes on the
newspaper for bankruptcy and distress auctions.   I've moved this
thread to alt.folklore.computers where it belongs (belongs??!); I had
posted a really lengthy followup before I noticed I wasn't in the
group I thought I was.  

