To all of my colleagues in the OpenVMS community, I wish to pass on some 
sad news which I received this morning:
     
     Cliff Fischer passed away on January 19, 1995 at his home.  He was 
     the Principal System Engineer for MTI Corporation attached to the 
     Sterling, Virginia office.  Cliff joined MTI in December 1992 from his 
     previous position as the System Manager for Co-Bank in Denver, Colorado.
     
     Cliff was very active in the local and national DECUS organizations.
     He was well known and liked by many who had attended his sessions at 
     DECUS, such as "Backup, Myths and Misconceptions, and I/O Tuning".
     
     Cliff's work centered around working with customers in technically 
     understanding their needs and advising them of multiple options for 
     consideration.  He also enjoyed performing benchmarks and remote 
     dial-ups for system analysis.
     
     Cliff spoke at numerous DECUS events in the U.S. as well as Europe.   
     Anyone desiring more information is welcomed to call Kevin Clark at 
     703-709-1122 or Internet: kclark@ccmgate.mti.com
 
I think that I speak for many of us when I say that we have all lost a good 
friend and generous colleague. Cliff's contributions and participation in 
DECUS, and the community in general will be missed.
 
- Bob
