>
>Farrell Woods (ftw@zk3.dec.com) wrote:
>: OSF V3.2 is available now!
> 
>  Is V3.2 a upgraded ver of 3.0x  , or a New ver ?

I don't understand your question.

DEC release numbers look like

  [Major].[Minor][Variant]

Since the thing that changed between 3.0x and 3.2 is the 'minor', 
you can call it a 'minor' release.

The difference between 3.0 and 3.0B is the 'variant'. Thus, 3.0B is a
'variant' release.  In general, variant releases *only* add support 
for new hardware.

The definitive document is the SPD (software product description)
which can be found on gatekeeper.dec.com/www.digital.com.

