kwulser@unlinfo.unl.edu (kurt wulser) writes:

}We are new to the Wacky World of VMS and need an easy way to determine
}the subdirectory size on a DEC 3000.  If possible, would like a batch
}file or single command for other novice users to determine the amount
}of space that they're using on the hard drive.  Tanks!

Since you are *new*, have you tried reading the documentation?  It is a
wonderful source of information especially to a new user.  Additionally, the
on-line help is a great way to learn.  Type HELP HINTS at the $ prompt for a
start.

There is also a FAQ in comp.answers you should read that contains basic
information new users find very useful.

Specifically, the command DIR/SIZE/TOTAL [SOMEDIRNAME] will give the users
information similar to what you seem to be asking.  This assumes that all of
their files are in the directory you specify.  If they have sub-directories,
the command DIR/SIZE/TOTAL [TOPDIRNAME...] will include all sub-directories as
well as a grand total.  If you wish a grand-total only, the command would be
DIR/SIZE/GRAND [TOPDIRNAME...]


