>Does anyone know it there exists an Amiga driver for this printer??? Or
>maybe a postscript emulation cartridge?? ...

DEC ANSI (a.k.a. DECansi, DEC PPL3, LN03 protocol) is a Digital printer control
language based on ANSI X3.64 for page printers. (It didn't catch on.)

I know that we don't provide Amiga drivers for any of our printers. Don't know
if anything else has been done.

There is an Adobe PostScript upgrade option for the DEClaser 2200 (which turns
it into what we call the DEClaser 2250). You may have to search around a bit to
find one since the model is several years old.
