In article <Bob1-2202951645400001@dial176.ibl.bm>, Bob1@IBL.BM (Martin J Walsh) writes:
> We have a FDDI based cluster with two main sites and a MicroVAX 3100 as a
> quorum machine at a 3rd site. All three sites have local shadowed system
> disks. All our applications have shadow sets with a member at each of the
> main sites. Some of these shadow sets are also mounted on the 3100.
> 
> We would like to control who manages shadow copies a little more than just
> the number of shadow copies. For example we only want the 3100 to perform
> shadow copies on its own disk not any other shadow sets from the main
> sites.

We've just been through this, and the answer we got from Digital is you can't
control it.  Any node in the cluster can initiate the shadow copy.  What we've
done is to initiate a dismount/mount sequence on the node we want the copy done
on.  This will force the local copy.  This is an issue I'd like to see Digital
address, perhaps with a SYSGEN parameter that restricts shadow copies to
locally-attached disks.

