If you let BAD run to completion, you have lost everything
with no hope of recovery.   If you managed to stop it before
it got very far, you might be able to recover some of the
data.

You have three options:  The first is to call an expert in
recovering data from ODS-1 disks.   The second is to buy a
commercial tool for this task and do it yourself.  The third
is to look on the *really* *old* RSX SIG tapes for tools called
DSKPAT, ERRCPY, UICREC and others in the same UIC.   This will
involve a lot of study and hand work, but involves the lowest
cash outlay.

The only commercial tool I know of is called RECOVR.   It
was written by Bruce Mitchell of Machine Intelligence and
Industrial Magic (MIIM).   He has recently moved and I
no longer know how to contact him.   Perhaps someone else
here can help us.

As for disk recovery experts, there are probably several
here on the net besides myself.   This is not a cheap
solution, but is certainly the fastest.

