I asked for information about how to transform a MV2000 into a VS2000
and vice versa.  My thanks to Tony Konashenok, Bob Armstrong, Sean
O'Banion and rmacklem@uoguelph.ca, who all sent me mail about this.

Here's a quick summary:

The right jumper sits a couple of inches directly behind the thinwire
connector on the main board.  There are three pins in line, and the
jumper connects the center pin to one of the two outer pins to select
the operating mode of the machine.  Simply swap the position of this
jumper to modify an MV into a VS or the other way around.

However, it seems that older models of the systems also need their
firmware ROMs replaced.  This wasn't so with my units, but be warned of
the possibility.

-tih


