> easy way out and just transform the VS into an MV and vice versa.


According to the VS/MV 2000 Technical Manual (#EK-VTTA-TM), the "system
jumper"  is in line with the Thinewire BNC connector: follow the axis of
the BNC connector towards the opposite side a couple of inches.  When the
two position jumper is towards the BNC connector, then the system is a MV;
when the jumper is away from the BNC connector, then the system is a VS.

Some place I remeber seeing some minimum ROM rev's that were different for
