Melinda,
      You probably already have a solution to this problem, but 
in case you don't, here is what I would try. I am doing this 
from memory since I am at home.

Shutdown or Halt the system. (break on the console should do 
it).

Boot the system in converstational mode

>>> b/r5:00000001

when you get the system up to the sysgen prompt, set STARTUP_P1 
to "MIN"

SYSGEN> SET STARTUP_P1 "MIN"

SYSGEN> CONT

The system will boot up in a minimum state and you should be 
able to clean up some files. I suggest you start by purging 
sys$manager:*.log. once you have enough files cleaned up, you 
should shut down the system, boot conversational again, reset 
STARTUP_P1 to "" nothing and type cont. Now you should have the 
full system up and can do a proper clean up. Hope this helps

Craig

