:Sorry if this was once a FAQ but the latest ULTRIX FAQ does not address it:
:
:The VR-260 on our venerable VS-3100/30 recently died in a spectacular fashion
:after being flooded by an overenthusiastic water distillation apparatus on the
:floor above.  I remember seeing (*years* ago) a discussion about how to drop a 
:VT-220 off one of the serial ports on the back of the system box and turning 
:it into a console.  As I recall, this involved setting a couple of the dip 
:switches and some other stuff.  Anybody remember the specifics?

  Power everything down, plug the MMJ serial line from the terminal into
  the VAXstation 3100 (the port with the printer icon), and flip the "S3"
  switch up, set the terminal to 9600 baud, power the expansion boxes up,
  power the system box up, and if you don't see >>> on the terminal press
  <BREAK>.  

  You can use the (semi-documented) DTE command to switch over to terminal
  emulation mode, and when in this mode you should now see the *>>> prompt
  -- use <CTRL/P> to get back to local console >>> mode. 

  With "S3" up, the system will always use the terminal as the console.

  Assuming the standard GPX graphics controller found in most VAXstation
  3100 model 30 systems, look at getting at least a VR262 (greyscale 19"
  60 Hz 1024 x 864) or VR297 (color 16" 60 Hz 1024 x 864) or VT299 (color
  19" 60 Hz 1024 x 864) -- these monitors replaced the VR260 and VR290
  monitors.

