>	about hardware flow control was... OSF1.
>
>	*** Is there any way to have RTS/CTS flow control? ***
>

  Yes, stty parameter is -clocal

     clocal implies a direct, hardwired link with Xon/Xoff flow control

    -clocal implies a modem connection with full modem control lines
            and hardware (RTS/CTS) flow control

>	Currently we cannot transfer any files with our
>	modem connection. I did fiddle with kermit parameters,
>	but nothing seems to help. This stinks!
>

  You should also check the modem setup parameters. If you're using a
mostly-Hayes compatible modem, the &K3 flag will set the modem to
hardware (RTS/CTS) flow control, &K0 will disable flow control altogether,
and &K4 will enable Xon/Xoff flow control. Different modem vendors have
different factory defaults.

