> Plug your VT220 into the Printer Port on the VS3100.  Find the tiny
> recessed slide switch near the Serial and Printer Ports and toggle
> it the other way.  Boot up with the VT220 at 9600 baud. You might
> have to bring up the VT220 Setup Menus and fiddle with parity, etc.
> Barry Kort

Watch out!  That dumb little switch doesn't have a hole cut in the back bezel
on some 3100's!  I had a friend that learned that the hard way.  We took the
case off & used a paperclip with about 2mm's worth bent over at 90� to flip
the switch because we didn't want to chew a hole in the bezel or tear up the
label that so conveniently covers the rear panel access screws.

Also! You will probably get 1 or 2 'soft' errors because the test code can't
test the serial port (or other various things).  Ignore them.  Sample text is:
Console test 50:
>>> test 50
 ? DZ       0000.4001
 ? SCSI-B   0000.4001  V1.58

Or bootup:
 ?  C  0080  0000.4001		<<< this line is untested, no error
 ?  6  80A1  0000.4001		<<< dma & interrupts untested, no error

I do wonder what they were smoking.....
