frequently. So the direction of traffic is from top to bottom.

Problem
-------

Slow response. The download rate is only 2Kbps (64kbps link !!!!!!).
Unacceptable.

Observation
-----------

We use the Sniffer at ethernt on DEC 2000 and find that there is a lot
of retransmission which is not due to bad CRC. A snapshot of DEC LAT
protocol is drafted as belows:


Frame   Delta T(ms)       T.S.                                      DEC
2000

1.      0.0000                SEQ 93, ACK 76, (Src, Dest ID 1), DATA
                         
<----------------------------------------------

2.      0.0023                SEQ 94, ACK 76, (Src, Dest ID 1), DATA
                         
<----------------------------------------------

3.      0.2537                SEQ 77, ACK 94, (Src, Dest ID 1), DATA
                          
---------------------------------------------->

4.      0.0004                SEQ 95, ACK 77, (Src, Dest ID 1), DATA
                         
<----------------------------------------------

5.      0.0023                SEQ 96, ACK 77, (Src, Dest ID 1), DATA
                         
<----------------------------------------------

6.      0.2041                SEQ 97, ACK 77, (Src, Dest ID 1),
(Padding)
                         
<----------------------------------------------

7.      0.0503                SEQ 78, ACK 96, (Src, Dest ID 1), DATA
                          
---------------------------------------------->
                                            �
                                            �
                                            �
                                            �
8.(*)   1.9494                SEQ 97(*), ACK 78, (Src, Dest ID 1), DATA
                         
<----------------------------------------------

A sample LAT header looks like:

Message type / flags = 00 (RUN from host, No response requested)
No. of slot = 1
Dest Circuit ID = 0015
Src Circuit ID = 3401

Dest Slot ID = 01
Source Slot ID = 01
Data Length = 126
Slot Type / Credits = 00

Frame 8 is a retransmission. All my protocol traces are filled with
this pattern. So the line is always silence for 2 sec frequently, which
slows down the transfer rate. I've made the following deduction based
on my observation, please correct me if I'me wrong.

1) The max. windows size of DEC 2000 is set to 3.

2) The max. window size of T.S. is set to 1.

3) The window mechanism of DEC LAT is some what strange. If DEC 2000
has 3 outstanding frames, the last one has to be acknowledged before
another 3 are sent out. Initially I expect when frame 7 acks frame 5,
DEC 2000 should send another 3 frames but it is not. And also since
max. win. size of T.S. is 1, when frame 7 is sent out, it has to wait
for ack from DEC 2000. Then deadlock comes in.

I've no idea of how DEC 2000 and T.S. can be configured. The solution
I'm thinking of are:

1) Bring DEC 2000 window size back to 2. Pls advise me what should be
done on DEC 2000.

2) Your suggestions are welcome but pls provide more configuration
details.

Remember nothing can be changed on the remote Transparent bridge.

Regards, Keith







                          


