  <F1> is often reserved for terminal-local functions and is not sent to
  the host system on various terminals.

  At least with the VT401-series keyboards, the <~`> can be reprogrammed
  to send <ESC>.  (This capability may also be available on various other
  keyboards -- you haven't mentioned which keyboard you have.)

  It's generally advantageous to reset the applications to use a key
  other than <ESC>, as that key typically does not appear in isolation
  on ANSI-compliant systems.  (I'll assume you are probably using vi
  or emacs -- emacs can definitely be remapped away from <ESC>.)

  If you prefer the UNIX or PC keyboard layouts, replacement LK4xx-series
  keyboards are available.

  Steve Lionel has already answered your `save settings' question.

