conditions.  Excessive retransmissions cause low effective throughput.  Now,
what in your configuration could cause excessive retransmissions?
 
A good candidate is the 64kb line.  Remember that this is kilobits per second. 
It sure looks to me like you should replace that slow line with something
faster before you bother with the software.  What you are really doing is
connecting two water mains t
ogether with a garden hose.
 
Networking software is usually quite sensitive to excessive round trip times. 
While the timers can be adjusted somewhat, the slow 64kb line can quite easily
cause a timeout, which then causes a retransmission, which then results in low
trhoughput.  After
all, the Ethernet segments run at 10mb which is quite a bit faster than 64kb.


