Tom Perrine (tep@galt.sdsc.edu) wrote:

: I have inherited a Personal DECstation 5000/25.  I know that there is
: at least one serial port, because that is currently (at this moment!)
: talking to a modem doing PPP.

: I have a printer that I also want to connect to this system.  It has
: centronics parallel and a serial port.

: Is there a second serial port (or parallel) "hidden" on the standard
: serial connector??

All the serial/printer ports on that series are MMJ connectors
(Modified Modular Jacks with the offset keytab).  They are usually
labeled with a pair of left/right arrows for serial ports, and
a printer icon for printer ports, and they are usually side by
side on the back panel.  It's possible that your model has but 
a single MMJ serial/printer port.

Barry Kort


