|> Can I install a generic SCSI-2 hard drive in the above machine (150MHz 
|> Alpha system)?

The simple answer is "yes" but you have to be aware of some stuff.

We don't do anything that precludes the use of non-DEC disks.  But
what you don't get with a non-DEC disk is a guarantee that it'll perform
the same or as well as a DEC-labeled disk.  So for instance if you
discovered that the Quantum drive had problems because they have a firmware
bug that causes the drive to violate the SCSI spec, then you would have
to convince Quantum to provide you with a fix.  We would not provide a
software patch to work around it in one of the three OS's.



