> VMS/Multinet.  Is there public domain software available to do this...if so 
> where?

OpenVMS and MultiNet combined include all you need to deliver mail.  OpenVMS
includes the standard MAIL utility, and you just use the SMTP% prefix for
delivering mail to the outside world.  You can also use the MX mailer for
additional functionality (like mailing lists, aliases, etc).  You can FTP MX
from ftp.spc.edu or ftp.wku.edu

MultiNet also includes MM, an alternative to VMSmail.  

For News, you need to decide if you want to run a server or just the client. 
For server software, your only alternative is ANU NEWS.  You can pick up the
distribution (I recommend at least 6.1b9) from kuhub.cc.ukans.edu.  There are a
set of patches on genetics.upenn.edu that can be applied to the 6.1b9 release. 
ANU News operates as both a client as well as a server.  Since you're in
Victoria, you may have access to the local DECUS LUG system.  If so, you can
check out ANU News running there (in client-only mode) as well as the MX
mailer.  E-mail me for details if you don't have access to the system.

For News clients, there are several alternatives.  You can check the software
list regularly posted to comp.os.vms.  NEWSRDR seems to be a popular choice. 
It's likely available on ftp.spc.edu as well.

