: The CX, which has a color screen works nicely, but the MX machine, which is
: monochrome, will not allow logins - the login screen comes up, but 
: the login immediately fails after entering the correct password.
: In the log-file of xdm on the Alpha each such failure leaves lines like this:

: > X Error of failed request:  BadAccess (attempt to access private resource denied)
: >   Major opcode of failed request:  88 (X_FreeColors)
: >   Serial number of failed request:  951
: >   Current serial number in output stream:  961

: Probably this is because of the lack of colors - yet monochrome VXT terminals
: have no such problem. Does anyone know how to make Ultrix tell OSF that
: the screen is monochrome and not color?

I would check the xdm-errors file in /usr/lib/X11/xdm.  I am suspecting 
something wrong with the Xsession file or somewhere around that.  Another
thing to try is to kill the xdm daemon and run it by hand with -debug (try
level 1 for now).  You'll see a whole bunch of debug messages coming at your
terminal and perhaps something obvious will occur. To help sort through this
you may want to redirect the debug output to a file.  Also, when I'm 
debugging an X terminal I'll sometimes remove the local X server startup
in the Xservers file (if you have one). This will remove a bunch of clutter
from the debug output.

You can also look in the .xsession-errors file in the user's directory.

