We are using rdump to backup several filesystems on a Sun SPARCstation 2
running Sun OS 4.1.1 onto the 4mm drive (TLZ06) of a DEC Alpha running
OSF/1 1.3.  The command lines executed from the Sun look something like
    rdump 0ubdsf 32 10000 60700 alpha:/dev/nrmt0h /usr
The d & s parameters were chosen to alllow the 4mm tape to be utilized
fully.  We backup nine file systems in this way with a script run by an
"at" job started at 2am once each week.

This procedure worked fine for several months, then it started to fail for
one or more of the filesystems in the list of nine.  The error is
    DUMP: Broken pipe
    DUMP: The ENTIRE dump is aborted
Wondering if it was a network problem, we isloated our small local network
from the "outside" world by disconnecting us from the bridge that serves
others in our building and connects us with the rest of the University.
Doing this for the last two weeks has enabled us to get complete backups
without any failures.

Our network people came in with a sniffer and found that prior to the error
in rdump shown above, the Alpha sent an IP packet to the Sun saying it had
a window size of 0 meaning that it could receive no more data.  Seeing
this, the Sun should have waited, but it didn't and tried to send some data
ti the Alpha.  The Alpha then sent a window of 65536 which is apparently
interpretted as a -1 signifying an (irrecoverable?) error condition.  From
then the two machines continued to sent packets back and forth without
accomplishing anything until rdump decided something was wrong and output
the above error message.

Although we now have a pretty good idea what is happening at the network/IP
level, we don't really understand how disconnecting us from the outside
world prevents the error from happening.  By the way, we have two other
machines (both Suns) that do a similar remote backup that have no problems.
 They are actually passing data over a much more congested part of the
network compared to our situation in which both machines are "local".

Is there a problem with doing rdump between two different machines running
different operating systems?  (There shouldn't be, I hope!)  Are there
known bugs in either of our systems for this operation?  Do we need to
rebuild either kernel with parameters that improve network performance?

Thanks for wading through such a long posting!  I will re-post any
interesting replies received via mail.

Thanks,
Peyton

