Britt Byrd <britt@vnet.net> wrote:
>
> Have installed the above Q-BUS and UNIBUS Ethernet devices and the
> problem we are seeing via a sniffer is all the devices have a Ethernet
> MAC address of zero??  Suggestions??


You don't say weither your running DECnet or IP or whatever. If it's
DECnet, when startnet executes, it changes the mac fron the hardware
address (08-00-2b-xx-xx-xx) to a aa-00-04-xx-xx-xx address you'll find
in the dlc header in the trace. It's labled Destination station and
Source station in the packet, just before the Ethertype (60-03).
The source DECnet address can also be found the drp layer after the
eco information. Make sure your sniffer in on the same subnet as the
traffic your looking at (not behind a router). Also, I would turn off
all capture filters and just take a trace of all traffic, then stop the
capture and filter on the capture. If it's DECnet you'll see a hello
(drp packet), if it's IP, just ping the router and look for that.
Also a question: How do you know this traffic is coming from the DELQA
if the mac is allways zero?




