In article <3h6kp1$uh8@nntp.Stanford.EDU>, hufnagel@popserver.stanford.edu (Todd C. Hufnagel) writes:
>I uncovered a rather nasty hardware error on one of my RZ57 disk drives
>while upgrading to Ultrix 4.4; since we no longer have a service
>contract I'm hoping someone can decipher this and give me an idea of
>how to proceed.
>
>One of the partitions went bad and couldn't be fixed by fsck.  When I
>ran rzdisk on that partition, it happily scanned blocks until the
>following error message came up:
>
>* ERROR OCCURED ON /dev/rrz0b DURING COMMAND (VERIFY DATA) *
>Sense key (0x4) hardware error
>Additional sense code (0x44): internal target failure
>Sense data: f0 0 4 0 1 7f ff c 0 0 0 0 44 0 e0 0 0 1

The ASC/ASCQ (Additional Sense Code, and Qualifier) is 4400, which translates
to (as was already displayed) "internal target failure".  The FRU code is E0.
I don't have the service manual for this drive to translate the FRU code to a
FRU unit.  However, I've seen FRU codes of E0 and D0, which I would figure
means the "electronics" and "drive" FRUs respectively.

What rev is the drive?  There may be a sticker on the side of the form Ann,
where 'A' is some letter, and 'nn' is a 2 digit number.  Also, from the console
prompt, get the firmware version number (like '5000' or '6000').  If the
firmware is less than '6000', or the rev of the drive is less than 'D01', then
there is an upgrade kit available.  The upgrade kit consists of a new firmware
ROM, and is part number EQ-01695-01.

However, since the drive has been running in the past, it's not likely that the
upgrade is going to fix the drive.  It may just be broke.

