:Does anyone knows the external clock speed for the ALPHA AXP chips?

  In the simplistic cases, the Alpha DECchip internal clock frequency is
  half of the external clock frequency -- a chip with an internal rating
  of 200 MHz can be driven at 400 MHz.

  Internal clock speeds can run at frequencies up to 300 MHz on announced
  DECchips (the 21164-300), though the frequency limit depends on the
  particular DECchip and on the particular system implementation.

  If you are planning on making more detailed enquiries or are considering
  an Alpha-based implementation, I would recommend acquiring the relevent
  DECchip micrprocessor manuals -- these manuals contain a wealth of detail
  on the implementation clocking options, etc.

