   I'll assume this is a VAXstation 3100 model 48, and if so, you likely
   simply need to set the SYSGEN parameter WINDOW_SYSTEM to 1.  (Place
   this parameter setting, and any other SYSGEN parameter changes you might
   happen to make, in the file SYS$SYSTEM:MODPARAMS.DAT.)  Reboot.

   The first error is due to the fact that the workstation display is little
   more than a glass TTY without a window system running on it -- rather
   than trying to log in and do any screen-oriented functions (which won't
   work on the "naked" workstation display), I'd use straight SYSEN to reset
   WINDOW_SYSTEM, WRITE CURRENT, and then reboot to get DECwindows running. 
   I'd then go back and edit MODPARAMS.

   V5.3 is relatively old, I'd look at upgrading to something a little more
   recent -- support will be rather easier.

