David Lloyd writes:

>int compare (int *a, int *b)

[snip]

>  qsort(intarray, 10, sizeof(int), compare);

>Line  305:        qsort(intarray, 10, sizeof(int), compare);
>%CC-W-PTRMISMATCH, In this statement, the referenced type of the pointer value
> "compare" is "function (...) returning int", which is not compatible with
> "function (...) returning int".

  The warning is complaining about the parameter types on your
function.  A qsort callback should take 'const void *' according to
the function prototype in stdlib.h

  Apparently, you have to declare your function with those types on
your parameters and then cast them to 'int *'.  If anybody else has a
better workaround, I'd be interested in hearing it.

