The back of the MV/VS 2000 has at least two connectors: SCSI for the
TZK50, and the external disk (MFM).

The SCSI chip, an NCR 5380, is supported on other systems as a SCSI port,
but not here.  You're only choice is the TZK50.  The part # for the
SCSI-to-TK50 is 54-17639-01 (TZK50-AA), says the spares list in the
Maintenance Guide.  The SCSI ID for the TZK50 MUST be 1 (jumper P1 & P2
installed, P3 open, as well as P4 installed (parity ?), otherwise the
driver (TVDRIVER.EXE) gets upset.

Carl Follstad is correct about Trimarchi...too bad Digital won't but
enough sources out for someone (like me) who would be willing to write a
SCSI port driver to then put into a DECUS library...


