> phase out some old Ultrix and VMS machines.

Possible?  Certainly.  You will need to write or find MOP download responder
code, and enough of the DECnet Phase IV infrastructure to support it.  The good
news is:

o	DECnet Phase IV documentation, at the level of detail that you need, is
	openly available for purchase from Digital.

o	DECnet is one of the socket families within the BSD socket interface
	architecture, and there may be Unix-flavored code available for free. 
	There is considerable work going on right now to specify DECnet for
	WinSockAPI, which is sort of an extension of BSD sockets, and you might
	find helpful experience there as well.

Sounds like fun.  I've been wishing that I had time to cook up a full-blown
DECnet Phase IV implementation for Linux.  A MOP downline loader/dump receiver
would be a nice small project to get it started.
