our AXPs.  The default installation provides appropriate keysym
translations to support the lispm's prodigous number of modifier keys (6,
at last count), but, while the supplied mappings are complete enough,
they're a bit lacking in usefulness.  In particular, each of the four
"standard" modifier keys on the LK401 are mapped to a different bucky key
on the virtual lispm.  Since I don't use "hyper", "super", or "symbol" a
whole heck of a lot, I used xmodmap to move these alternate modifiers to
top-row F-keys, replacing the original mappings with other, more useful
modifiers (pairs of meta- and controls, as occur on Symbolics physical
keyboards).

On the whole, I seem to have gotten most of it to work (swapped mod
mappings, wrote a wee xclient to disable autorepeat on the F-key
modifiers), but I'm stuck with one remaining obstacle: there's a particular
chord that just doesn't work, specifically "F4-Shift-L" (where F4 is mapped
to mod3 with xmodmap).  I get no KeyPress or KeyRelease events with xev.
However, things like "F4-Shift-K" and "F4-Shift-;" work just fine. Plus,
other keys, like F7, which are also mapped to mod3 also work (F7-Shift-L
works ok!)

It occurs under both mwm and dxsession.  There may be other "dead chords" like
this, but I haven't found any (don't have the time to physically test all
2^6 * Nkeys permuations!).

Does anyone have any suggestions or theories about what might be going on
here? I'm mystified, particularly due to the rather singular nature of the
behavior.

Thanks,
pete




